WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.350 --> 00:00:02.183
- My band is since "Idol."

00:00:02.183 --> 00:00:03.392
Most of them.
- Are you kidding me?

00:00:03.392 --> 00:00:04.371
- [Kelly] Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:00:04.371 --> 00:00:05.691
Especially Jason.
- I love it.

00:00:05.691 --> 00:00:06.597
- Yeah, yeah, yeah.
- Hi, guys!

00:00:06.597 --> 00:00:08.343
- You smell good!
(audience cheering)

00:00:08.343 --> 00:00:09.176
- Thanks, Angel.
- Angel!

00:00:09.176 --> 00:00:10.110
I was like that star thing.

00:00:10.110 --> 00:00:10.943
Yeah, I love that.

00:00:10.943 --> 00:00:12.090
It smells so good.
- She said "The star thing."

00:00:12.090 --> 00:00:13.380
- It looks like the little star thing.

00:00:13.380 --> 00:00:14.250
- It does.
- Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:00:14.250 --> 00:00:15.390
- And I spray so much of it

00:00:15.390 --> 00:00:17.700
that I go through a
bottle like in two weeks.

00:00:17.700 --> 00:00:18.533
- You know what?

00:00:18.533 --> 00:00:19.712
I can't do it.

00:00:19.712 --> 00:00:21.570
It doesn't last on me.

00:00:21.570 --> 00:00:23.237
I spray perfume and nobody's ever, like...

00:00:23.237 --> 00:00:25.581
- You're not spraying enough, Kels.

00:00:25.581 --> 00:00:26.632
- [Kelly] I know, but then I feel like...

00:00:26.632 --> 00:00:27.760
- You gotta (imitating spray bottle).

00:00:27.760 --> 00:00:28.593
- Okay, I'm not good at it.

00:00:28.593 --> 00:00:29.580
I need lessons.

00:00:29.580 --> 00:00:31.920
Congratulations on the Golden Globe nom.

00:00:31.920 --> 00:00:33.472
That's incredible.
- Thank you.

00:00:33.472 --> 00:00:34.981
(audience cheering and applauding)

00:00:34.981 --> 00:00:36.472
Oh my God.

00:00:36.472 --> 00:00:39.210
- I mean we're both from the same show.

00:00:39.210 --> 00:00:40.043
You know what I'm saying?

00:00:40.043 --> 00:00:42.480
So it's like, I never
thought I'd be doing this.

00:00:42.480 --> 00:00:43.710
You never thought, like
I never even thought

00:00:43.710 --> 00:00:44.640
I'd be in an Emmy category.

00:00:44.640 --> 00:00:46.740
Never think you'd be in these categories

00:00:46.740 --> 00:00:47.573
that we're in.
- No.

00:00:47.573 --> 00:00:49.380
- Like is this just blowing your mind?

00:00:49.380 --> 00:00:50.340
- It's like a dream.

00:00:50.340 --> 00:00:51.660
Like when my husband...

00:00:51.660 --> 00:00:52.830
I was in LA.

00:00:52.830 --> 00:00:55.620
I was stuck in LA, I was
supposed to be in New York.

00:00:55.620 --> 00:00:58.050
And yeah, they kept
pushing the flight back.

00:00:58.050 --> 00:01:00.990
But my husband, we talk every morning.

00:01:00.990 --> 00:01:02.070
That's my best friend.

00:01:02.070 --> 00:01:05.670
And I called home and
everybody was screaming.

00:01:05.670 --> 00:01:06.871
So I hung up.

00:01:06.871 --> 00:01:10.040
(all laughing)

00:01:10.040 --> 00:01:11.360
- It is too early.

00:01:11.360 --> 00:01:12.420
- 'Cause I thought something was wrong.

00:01:12.420 --> 00:01:13.680
- Oh, you were like, "No bad news."

00:01:13.680 --> 00:01:14.670
- No bad news.

00:01:14.670 --> 00:01:17.730
So I called back and I'm like,
"Baby, you gotta calm down.

00:01:17.730 --> 00:01:18.563
Tell me what's wrong."

00:01:18.563 --> 00:01:21.180
He's like, "You got nominated
for a Golden Globe!"

00:01:21.180 --> 00:01:23.451
And literally, here's what I did.

00:01:23.451 --> 00:01:26.240
(Fantasia sobbing)
- Oh my God!

00:01:26.240 --> 00:01:28.110
My favorite part is that you hung up.

00:01:28.110 --> 00:01:29.640
- (laughing) I had to.
- Bye.

00:01:29.640 --> 00:01:33.150
- I didn't know that something
like this could happen for...

00:01:33.150 --> 00:01:34.440
You know, we just love to sing.

00:01:34.440 --> 00:01:35.273
- That's what I'm saying.

00:01:35.273 --> 00:01:36.600
You had like a dream
and then it kind of...

00:01:36.600 --> 00:01:38.490
You said yes to opportunities that made...

00:01:38.490 --> 00:01:40.440
Well actually, you didn't
say yes to this opportunity

00:01:40.440 --> 00:01:41.273
at first.
- No.

00:01:41.273 --> 00:01:43.560
- Which is crazy to me
because you play her

00:01:43.560 --> 00:01:44.700
on Broadway.
- Broadway.

00:01:44.700 --> 00:01:46.050
- You're incredible on Broadway.

00:01:46.050 --> 00:01:47.940
And like, it seems like
such a natural progression.

00:01:47.940 --> 00:01:48.773
Why'd you say no at first?

00:01:48.773 --> 00:01:50.613
- It was so heavy on Broadway, Kels.

00:01:51.538 --> 00:01:52.770
- [Kelly] Just day in, day out, that roll?

00:01:52.770 --> 00:01:56.790
- Eight shows a week, plus
my life was a bit crazy then.

00:01:56.790 --> 00:01:59.580
So it felt like I was carrying
my cross and her cross.

00:01:59.580 --> 00:02:01.410
- Yeah.
- And that was a overload.

00:02:01.410 --> 00:02:02.243
- Yeah.

00:02:02.243 --> 00:02:04.447
- And so this time when
Scott called, I was thinking,

00:02:04.447 --> 00:02:07.290
"Did you not see all the interviews

00:02:07.290 --> 00:02:09.800
when I said I would never ever come back?"

00:02:09.800 --> 00:02:10.633
(all laughing)

00:02:10.633 --> 00:02:12.330
- Felt challenged by it.
- Yeah.

00:02:12.330 --> 00:02:15.210
And he just said, you
know, "You're our Celie."

00:02:15.210 --> 00:02:18.750
Our director, Blitz, he
called and when he told me

00:02:18.750 --> 00:02:22.440
he was giving Celie an
imagination, I said, "I'm in."

00:02:22.440 --> 00:02:24.360
Because we all have an imagination

00:02:24.360 --> 00:02:26.100
and when we're in bad places,

00:02:26.100 --> 00:02:28.530
we imagine ourselves in better places.

00:02:28.530 --> 00:02:29.700
- Yeah, you need it.
- Yeah.

00:02:29.700 --> 00:02:31.110
So I was like, "I'm all in."

00:02:31.110 --> 00:02:32.400
On Broadway, you didn't get to see

00:02:32.400 --> 00:02:34.590
how she worked out her stuff.

00:02:34.590 --> 00:02:36.562
She goes through, goes
through, goes through and then,

00:02:36.562 --> 00:02:37.395
♪ And I'm here ♪

00:02:37.395 --> 00:02:38.340
And everybody's like, "Yay!"

00:02:38.340 --> 00:02:40.530
But how did you get here?
- Yeah.

00:02:40.530 --> 00:02:42.330
- So I was just very excited

00:02:42.330 --> 00:02:43.560
that they gave her an imagination.

00:02:43.560 --> 00:02:44.574
- Yeah.

00:02:44.574 --> 00:02:45.552
(audience cheering and applauding)

00:02:45.552 --> 00:02:48.770
And it's hard when you're
going through life stuff.

00:02:48.770 --> 00:02:49.860
I was talking to Jason about that too.

00:02:49.860 --> 00:02:50.790
You go through life stuff

00:02:50.790 --> 00:02:53.160
and you have to compartmentalize
and also do your job.

00:02:53.160 --> 00:02:54.057
So that's hard.
- It's hard.

00:02:54.057 --> 00:02:55.230
- And when you're in a better place

00:02:55.230 --> 00:02:56.700
you're like, "I won't go there.

00:02:56.700 --> 00:02:57.622
Why would I do that?"

00:02:57.622 --> 00:02:58.709
Get it, get it, get it, get it.

00:02:58.709 --> 00:03:01.110
(audience cheering and applauding)

00:03:01.110 --> 00:03:04.020
Do you, I'm just curious,
'cause I was forced to,

00:03:04.020 --> 00:03:06.870
'cause I had to do something
and say yes to something.

00:03:06.870 --> 00:03:08.430
Like to let them see it.

00:03:08.430 --> 00:03:10.260
Have you ever seen you on "Idol?"

00:03:10.260 --> 00:03:11.940
Do you ever watch yourself on "Idol?"

00:03:11.940 --> 00:03:13.050
Like, have you ever done that?

00:03:13.050 --> 00:03:13.883
- I do.

00:03:13.883 --> 00:03:16.149
You know, a good glass of
wine always sends me back.

00:03:16.149 --> 00:03:16.982
(audience laughing)

00:03:16.982 --> 00:03:17.815
I kid you not.
- Girl.

00:03:17.815 --> 00:03:19.501
- My husband's here.

00:03:19.501 --> 00:03:21.440
I will literally go back.

00:03:21.440 --> 00:03:23.600
(audience applauding)

00:03:23.600 --> 00:03:27.150
Now, and I dunno if you like
me, I hate watching myself.

00:03:27.150 --> 00:03:29.970
- I hate watching myself.
- With a passion.

00:03:29.970 --> 00:03:32.880
But if I've had a good glass of cab...

00:03:32.880 --> 00:03:34.440
(audience laughing)

00:03:34.440 --> 00:03:37.320
- There's not enough
wine in the world to...

00:03:37.320 --> 00:03:38.670
Like literally I watched it.

00:03:38.670 --> 00:03:39.720
I had to watched it and I found...

00:03:39.720 --> 00:03:43.170
Dude, I feel like if I got
through that I can do anything.

00:03:43.170 --> 00:03:44.310
Yes, anything.

00:03:44.310 --> 00:03:46.560
- Gimme another one.
- Anything, anything.

00:03:46.560 --> 00:03:48.381
I was like, "I did that."

00:03:48.381 --> 00:03:49.749
And it was hard, I was tired.

00:03:49.749 --> 00:03:50.582
- Yes.

00:03:50.582 --> 00:03:52.200
I was over it a lot.
- I know.

00:03:52.200 --> 00:03:55.117
Anyway, let's do another short
commercial break, everybody.

00:03:55.117 --> 00:03:57.240
"The Color Purple" is in
theaters Christmas day.

00:03:57.240 --> 00:03:58.490
Y'all gotta check it out.

